  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TAKING ACTION TO COMBAT THE ILLEGAL TRADE AND EXPLOITATION OF MARINE TURTLES IN VIETNAM, PHASE II</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO SUPPORT IMPLEMENTATION OF THE NATIONAL MARINE TURTLE CONSERVATION PLAN OF VIETNAM AND TO BUILD CAPACITY FOR THE VIETNAMESE GOVERNMENT TO RESPOND TO ILLEGAL SEA TURTLE TRAFFICKING. PROJECT ACTIVITIES INCLUDE: (1) WORKING CLOSELY WITHIN THE DIRECTORATE OF FISHERIES TO FACILITATE IMPLEMENTATION OF CONSERVATION ACTIONS IDENTIFIED IN THE ACTION PLAN, SUCH AS ORGANIZING AND HOLDING WORKSHOPS WITH STAKEHOLDERS TO DEVELOP TIMELINES AND COMMITMENTS FOR SPECIFIC CONSERVATION ACTIONS IDENTIFIED IN THE PLAN (2) CONDUCT ANNUAL MARKET SURVEYS IN TRADE HOTSPOTS LIKE HANOI, HO CHI MINH CITY, NHA TRANG, DAN NANG, CON DAO ISLAND, AND PHU QUOC ISLAND (3) IMPLEMENTING AN AWARENESS CAMPAIGN TARGETED TOWARDS THE FISHING INDUSTRY AND (4) CONDUCTING TRAINING WORKSHOPS WITH THE GOVERNMENT AUTHORITIES AND SCIENTIFIC AGENCIES ON THE ELEMENTS OF THE SHELLBANK DATABASE, INCLUDING NEW IDENTIFICATION, INDICTMENT AND INVESTIGATION TECHNOLOGIES.</narrative>
  </description>
